{
 "item": {
  "title": "Millcreek tree canopy",
  "type": "Web Map",
  "snippet": "Canopy cover by ownership zone, and lidar tree crowns and treetops by height, over imagery. Unvalidated LiDAR planning estimates from the 2023 Salt Lake Valley QL1 lidar (flown October-November 2023); not surveyed or field-verified data.",
  "description": "<p><b>Unvalidated LiDAR planning estimates from the 2023 Salt Lake Valley QL1 lidar (flown October-November 2023); not surveyed or field-verified data.</b></p><p>At city scale: canopy cover (vegetation at least 2 m tall, as a share of the area the lidar observed) for each ownership zone; click a zone for its figure, bounds and the October 19 comparison. Zoom in past 1:20,000 for the tree crowns and, from 1:10,000, the treetops, coloured and sized by treetop height. The lidar hillshade is blended over the imagery (soft light).</p><p>Treetops and crowns are unvalidated automatic detections; about 6% of treetops carry an unreviewed SUSPECT flag.</p><p><b>Treetop height (crowns and treetops):</b> <span style='color:#D9F0A3'>■</span> 2 to 5 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#ADDD8E'>■</span> 5 to 10 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#78C679'>■</span> 10 to 15 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#31A354'>■</span> 15 to 20 m &nbsp; <span style='color:#006837'>■</span> 20 m and over; larger treetop dots are taller trees.</p><p>Crowns and treetops are vector tiles: they draw but have no pop-ups, and the map legend cannot list them (the key above stands in).</p><p>Datum: NAD83(2011) taken to WGS84 / Web Mercator with WGS_1984_(ITRF08)_To_NAD_1983_2011, the same for every layer. Records: canopy-toolbox/reviews/2026-10-23/agol-styling in buschbrian/agol-python-scripts.</p>",
  "tags": [
   "Millcreek",
   "lidar",
   "2023",
   "planning estimate",
   "canopy",
   "tree canopy",
   "trees",
   "treetops",
   "crowns"
  ],
